      "message": "Would it be better if we keep constant bytes (`salt_rkp_vm` which is orthogonal to the salt) to be added incase `rkp_vm_marker` is set and not add it in cases of non RKPVM OSes?\n\nThe rationale for the suggestion is that while pvmfw should be differentiating secrets of the new/higher privileged OS but it shouldn\u0027t be affecting the Hidden Inputs of u-droid, which (as per spec) should be stable across updates.\nIf possible, we\u0027d like to avoid the pattern of changing secrets* of older DICE paths when DICE chains are forked as a result of new features (or new OSes with different capabilities are introduced).\n\n[Side Q: Is the marker set false in the config descriptor for `vm_entry` node in u-droid DICE chain]\n\n*Even though devices cannot really use there stable Sealing CDIs without Secretkeeper.\n\n\nSorry the recommendation in b/323523191 wasn\u0027t clear on this bit, I meant it in spirit of changing secrets, but didn\u0027t suggest exact mechanism",
